From b45e74fd590590e274c15feb62a2229024c27d95 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 08:46:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: Program frame geometry for VFE 4.1 RDI

MSM8226's VFE 4.0 uses the 4.1 operations and needs the frame-based write
master buffer geometry programmed as well as the frame-based mode bit.
Carry the existing integration change 80d26059f27d onto media-committers
next, following the ARM32 DMA prerequisite 053ff674a48f.

Add an optional gen1 geometry callback and set it for the 4.1 operations.
Program words per line, height minus one, and burst length before taking
ownership of queued buffers or enabling the write master. Reject geometry
that cannot fit the 12-bit height and 16-bit word-count fields. The pinned
vendor MSM8226 driver programs the same register fields and burst value.

Advertise and negotiate the 4096-line bound on this RDI path through both
VFE subdev formats and capture-node formats. Carry the bound from gen1
operations to the video node. Other gen1 generations retain their generic
limit, and PIX keeps its existing line-based format behaviour. Keep the
bounds check before buffer consumption so an invalid direct configuration
cannot leave buffers owned by an output that failed to start.

The host qualification executes the actual enable, address initialization,
frame-drop, register, format and enumeration functions with synthetic core
services. It compares 756 RDI cases with the pinned vendor geometry code,
checks all seven write masters and three RDI lines, and exercises zero,
one and two queued buffers. The 6433 checks include TRY/ACTIVE, capture
limits, invalid geometry, optional callbacks, PIX and a modeled restart.
There are 1759 failed checks before the change and none afterward. Six
regression controls fail as expected. Full registration, the V4L2 IOCTL
core, PM, ISR interaction and physical capture are not executed. Native
ARM and ARM64 CAMSS component builds use W=1 and COMPILE_TEST disabled.

This is a prerequisite for the proposed MSM8226 support, rather than a
claim of physical qualification on every VFE 4.1 platform. No upstream
Fixes attribution is invented for the original out-of-tree feature.
Physical V4L2 compliance and image integrity remain pending.

Timothy Schmidt authored 80d26059f27d with Claude Opus 5.5, credited as
co-author <noreply@anthropic.com> in that history. OpenAI Codex (GPT-6)
ported the feature, added field bounds and format-limit propagation, and
prepared the source-bound models and local qualification. Human review
and DCO certification remain pending.
